# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for meshio++ (roadmap 3.9.1).
#
# Every entry here must explain why it is a known third-party false positive
# (not a race in meshio++'s own code). Leave empty unless a concrete third-party
# runtime frame is observed under TSan.

# Ubuntu's system libtbb12 (oneTBB) is not compiled with -fsanitize=thread, so
# TSan cannot observe synchronization inside libtbb.so / tbb::detail::d1
# work-stealing (e.g. dynamic_grainsize_mode::check_being_stolen in partitioner.h).
race:tbb::detail::
called_from_lib:libtbb.so
